14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not a listed building and is not covered by a tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the design (such as the glazing pattern or opening style), you will likely need to apply first.

Before you start, I'd suggest:
- Comparing your proposed windows with the existing ones in material and pattern.
- Speaking with the planning desk if you're unsure whether your plans count as a like-for-like replacement. I can't give a formal opinion on whether permission is needed. That decision rests with the council.

If you already have an application reference for this work, send it to me and I can check its status.
